---
const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Where do I get my DKIM key?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "From your sending service: Gmail, Microsoft 365, and ESPs generate the key pair and show you the public value to publish. The private key never leaves their system in hosted setups." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Can I add DKIM without my ESP?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Only if you run your own mail server and generate the key pair yourself. Hosted ESPs own the private key and publish the selector for you to add." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "How do I test the record after adding it?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Send a message and read the DKIM result in its headers, or run the selector through our DKIM record checker before sending anything." } }
  ],
};
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

---
<BaseLayout title="How to Add a DKIM Record (Any Provider)" description="How to add a DKIM record step by step: get the selector and key from your sending service, publish the TXT record, and verify it."  
 breadcrumb={[["Home", "/"], ["DNS Guide", "/dns/"], ["Add DKIM Record"]]}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/dns/" class="hover:text-accent">DNS Guide</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">Add DKIM Record</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">How to Add a DKIM Record</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      DKIM setup is a copy-precision exercise: your sending service hands you a selector and a public
      key, you publish them as a TXT record at selector._domainkey, you verify. Here is the whole
      procedure with the failure points marked.
    </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">DKIM record fields</h2>
    <section class="not-prose my-4" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="pdns-table" style="width:100%">
          <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Example value</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">Host / Name</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">s1._domainkey</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Selector plus the fixed _domainkey label</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">Type</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">TXT</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">DKIM keys publish as TXT (some hosts use CNAME)</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">Value</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=MIIB...</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">The public key, verbatim from your provider</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">TTL</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">3600</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Standard caching</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2>Step by step</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li><strong>Get the values from your sender.</strong> Google Workspace, Microsoft 365, and every ESP generate the key pair and show you: the selector (host name fragment), and the TXT value starting <code>v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=...</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Create the TXT record</strong> in your DNS host. Host/name: <code>selector._domainkey</code> (your provider may show the full <code>selector._domainkey.yourdomain.com</code>). Value: the key string verbatim. TTL 3600.</li>
        <li><strong>Do not touch the key.</strong> No added spaces, no smart quotes, no truncation. If the value exceeds 255 characters your DNS host either splits it automatically or expects multiple quoted strings.</li>
        <li><strong>Activate signing on the sender side.</strong> Publishing DNS does nothing until the service starts signing; in Google Workspace you must click "Start authentication", in M365 run Enable-DkimSigning.</li>
        <li><strong>Verify end to end.</strong> The <a href="/dkim-record-checker/">DKIM checker</a> confirms the key resolves and reports its strength; then send yourself a message and check the <code>DKIM-Signature</code> header plus the receiver's <code>Authentication-Results</code>.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2>Common failure points</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Host written as <code>_domainkey</code> alone, dropping the selector: wrong name, no resolution.</li>
        <li>Key pasted with the quotes some panels add automatically, doubling them.</li>
        <li>DNS published but sender-side signing never enabled: everything checks out except actual mail.</li>
        <li>Multiple senders sharing one selector: they must each use their own.</li>
      </ul>
      
<h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Where do I get my DKIM key?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">From your sending service: Gmail, Microsoft 365, and ESPs generate the key pair and show you the public value to publish. The private key never leaves their system in hosted setups.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I add DKIM without my ESP?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Only if you run your own mail server and generate the key pair yourself. Hosted ESPs own the private key and publish the selector for you to add.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I test the record after adding it?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Send a message and read the DKIM result in its headers, or run the selector through our DKIM record checker before sending anything.</p></details></div>
      <h2>Related</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/dkim/">DKIM explained</a> and <a href="/dkim-selector/">selectors</a></li>
        <li><a href="/dmarc/">DMARC: the layer above</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
